      "findings": [
        "mac_selinux_setup skips an initrd without its SELinux configuration directory.",
        "service_add_fd_store performs fstat before accepting a deserialized descriptor; failure consumes/closes that descriptor.",
        "udevd creates a fresh NETLINK_KOBJECT_UEVENT socket in manager_serialize_events, stores queued events in it, and sends event-serialization only if at least one event was stored.",
        "On the new invocation, manager_listen_fds handles the named storage socket separately from systemd-udevd-kernel.socket.",
        "The default init label calculation uses getfilecon on the executable. A newc archive does not supply its old SELinux xattrs.",
        "The standard relabel-extra hook runs before manager startup, but a prepacked /run drop-in would be hidden when /run is mounted; it is not the chosen implementation."
      ]
